From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leszek Swirski <leszeks@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:37:13 +0200
Subject: [interpreter] Check max_arguments stack space before Sparkplug OSR

InterpreterEntryTrampoline only checks BytecodeArray::frame_size_ on
function entry because Ignition call helpers check stack space before
pushing outgoing call arguments. Sparkplug, by contrast, relies on
BaselineOutOfLinePrologue pre-checking BytecodeArray::max_frame_size()
(frame_size_ + max_arguments_) at function entry and pushes outgoing
arguments at call sites without a stack check. When a function entered
in Ignition near the stack limit OSRs into Sparkplug inside a loop,
InterpreterOnStackReplacement_ToBaseline bypasses the baseline prologue,
allowing subsequent calls with many arguments to push past real_jslimit
and real_climit.

In InterpreterAssembler::OnStackReplacement, verify that there is enough
remaining stack space for max_arguments_ before tail-calling
InterpreterOnStackReplacement_ToBaseline, continuing the loop in
Ignition if not.

TAG=agy
CONV=8ac6e096-bff0-46cd-8db3-1f8046c78ca3

Fixed: 563716534
